## Lore

Loss Prevention Officers are Northern Gun''s private army of spies, enforcers and specialists, known to outsiders as Northern Gun Special Forces. They conduct tactical strikes and intelligence gathering against Naruni Enterprises and other alien competitors, lead most of the corporation''s military operations, and take every mission too sensitive to trust to mercenaries or local law enforcement. Answering only to the heads of the corporation and Ishpeming''s top political leaders, they are arresting officers, commandos, spies, and often judge, jury and executioner.

Despite that authority, LPOs are notorious "boy scouts": loyal first to Northern Gun the corporation and second to the Ishpeming Republic, sincere about justice and security, and mostly beyond bribes. They are stationed at every official Northern Gun city and major commercial center, can commandeer company property, and may pose as Sales Representatives, Operators, service personnel, managers, IMCN mercs, local authorities or customers.

Alignment: Any, but 35% are Unprincipled and 40% Scrupulous. All official Loss Prevention Officers are human.

## Equipment

A Northern Gun rifle of choice and pistol of choice with five extra E-Clips for each, an NG-H5 Holdout ion pistol, one NG Power Pack (any type), NG-S2 survival kit, two LPO field uniforms (black with grey trim), an LPO dress uniform, LPO I.D. and credentials, NG body armor of choice, walkie-talkie, nightvision goggles, 2 auditory listening bugs, 1 micro-video camera, field computer, compass, canteen and hiking boots.

LPOs have nearly unlimited access to Northern Gun products on special assignment, including vehicles, explosives, giant combat robots and aircraft, when the allocation is justified to an LPO Team Supervisor, a Department Head or Chief Callister, and the officer is trusted with it. G.M.s, use your discretion.

## Pay and cybernetics

Pay is 6,000 NGMI credits a month; characters start with one month''s pay.

LPOs often have 1D6+1 cybernetic implants or minor bionics, and the company pays for bionic or Bio-System replacements for parts lost in the line of duty. All bionic augmentation must be authorized by the company, though as many as eight legal cybernetic enhancements are allowed. Only 4% are partial cyborgs and there are no Combat Cyborgs on the force.

## GM Notes

LPO Chief: Andrea Callister. Department heads printed with the class include Michael J. Osborne (Acquisitions and Recovery), Ed Surrett (Alien Investigations), Denny "Kegleneq" Ham (Corporate Assets), Ryan Rawlings (Espionage), Stephen Daniel (Intelligence), Doctor Winston (Interrogations, a Rogue Scientist), Patrick Le Houllier (Investigations), Greg Diaczyk (National Security), Jeremy Davis (Special Ops), Ralph Lajara (Tactical Strikes & Counter-insurgency), Jeff A. Lee (Threat Assessment & Eradication) and Thomas Karras (Undercover Ops).
